-- Migration 0007 — Phase 6 ecommerce tables: product categories,
-- products, product images, product variants, inventory movements,
-- carts + cart items, customer addresses, orders, order items and
-- order status history (DATABASE_DESIGN.md §9.1–§9.10; the invoice
-- tables of §10 are Phase 7 and are NOT created here).
-- Generated by drizzle-kit from src/database/schema/store.ts and
-- hand-adjusted per DATABASE_DESIGN.md §13.1:
--   1. Every CREATE TABLE carries the design §2.1 table options
--      ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci.
--   2. Boolean columns are written in the design's literal form
--      tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0/1 (drizzle emitted
--      `boolean ... DEFAULT false/true`); same adjustment as
--      0000/0003/0005.
--   3. drizzle-kit also emitted DROP/re-ADD statements for the three
--      circular pages ↔ page_revisions FKs under auto-generated names,
--      plus a DROP of the hand-written FULLTEXT index ft_news_search:
--      the known phantom diffs (see 0005's header, items 3 and 5).
--      All of them were removed here, and the design FK names /
--      ft_news_search were restored in meta/0007_snapshot.json. A
--      future `db:generate` may re-emit those phantom diffs — remove
--      them the same way.
--   4. Tables are created in dependency order (categories → products
--      → images/variants → carts → cart items → addresses → orders →
--      order items → status history → movements); all FKs are added
--      by ALTER TABLE once every table exists. inventory_movements is
--      created last because it references orders (§9.5's
--      migration-order note).
--   5. RECORDED DEVIATION 1 (Phase 6, the BD-2 bridge of Phase 5):
--      product_images.media_id is NULLABLE and the table carries a
--      legacy `image_url` column — the Gift Shop's imagery is remote
--      Unsplash URLs pending the client's media decision. See the
--      header of src/database/schema/store.ts.
--   6. RECORDED DEVIATION 2 (Phase 0 amendment A1, superseding §9.5's
--      D3 note): inventory_movements.movement_type gains RESERVE and
--      RELEASE — checkout reserves stock at order creation instead of
--      deducting it. The full availability model (available =
--      stock_qty + SUM of RESERVE/RELEASE quantities, fulfilment
--      writes ORDER_DEDUCT + RELEASE as a pair) is documented in the
--      header of src/database/schema/store.ts.
--   7. Amendment A2 (order idempotency) needed NO change here:
--      §9.8 already specifies orders.idempotency_key with
--      uq_orders_idempotency (user_id, idempotency_key).
-- Rollback: 0007_store_down.sql (same folder).
